# `.env*` rather than a list of names: enumerating them left .env.vps and
# .env.prod unprotected, and DEPLOYMENT.md tells the reader to copy from
# .env.production.example, so a differently-named env file is likely. Same
# fix already applied to .gitignore.
#
# Heavy, git-ignored working directories that must never enter the build
# context — .postgres/ alone is a fully extracted portable PostgreSQL
# install (hundreds of MB) living inside the repo.
node_modules
.next
.git
.env*
.postgres
.pgdata
.superpowers

# Reference/design material and docs — never built, never shipped.
design
docs
*.md
PBK - Pencatatan Buku Kas.html

# Tests and their artifacts — not needed inside the image.
tests
test-results
playwright-report

# Deployment files themselves — the image doesn't need to COPY its own
# recipe, and docker-compose*.yml never belongs inside an image.
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
Caddyfile
